From 28a6f075bce8b1a59f56a99be947d5232671f7c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:39:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Install a device recipe the install media carries

A USB creator that recognises the machine can put a recipe on the
OMARCHY_FW partition: a pacman repository's packages with its database,
its signing key, and which packages to install. The installer installs
them with the system, from the media with dependencies from the offline
mirror, the recipe's repository first so a kernel it carries replaces
Omarchy's before the UKI is built. The repository then goes above
[omarchy] in the installed pacman.conf with its key trusted, so updates
keep coming. When something the packages need is not on the media, a
first-boot service installs them once the machine is online.

Recipes are validated before anything reads them: repository names that
are Omarchy's own or could break pacman.conf, plain-HTTP servers, short
fingerprints and odd package names are refused. Unit tests pass (183).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
